    "result_text": "All 12 test classes (the 12 `Cp*Tests` acceptance classes; `AuditLogCapture` and `AcceptanceBase` are helpers) ran, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization in the owner-creation flow in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`.\n\n**New helper \u2014 `normalizeAddress(String)`:**\n- Trims and collapses whitespace runs to a single space\n- Upper-cases\n- Expands common street abbreviations via a `Map`: `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE` (token-wise, so only whole words are expanded)\n- Returns `\"\"` for null/blank input, and is idempotent (an already-normalized address maps to itself)\n\n**Changes to `addOwner`:**\n1. The address is normalized once at the top, and the required-field check now rejects an address that is **blank after normalization** (`isBlank(normalizedAddress)`), so whitespace-only input yields a 400.\n2. Household-duplicate detection and the shared `householdId` derivation now use the normalized address (`normalizeAddress(existing.getAddress())` for stored owners, which is robust regardless of when they were created).\n3. The owner is stored \u2014 and therefore returned \u2014 with the normalized address via `owner.setAddress(normalizedAddress)`.\n\nThis satisfies the spec and all tests: `Cp12` (whitespace/case normalization, abbreviation expansion, blank-after-normalize rejection), `Cp10` (duplicate detection on normalized addresses \u2192 409), and `Cp11` (same `householdId` for normalized-equal addresses), plus all pre-existing tests remain green.",
